  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[0].trans": "722.6 (5G-TRONIC, 5-speed automatic)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[0].spec": "MB 236.10 (236.12 / 236.14 also acceptable)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[0].alternatives[2].brand": "Liqui Moly",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[0].note": "Fuchs's Chinese website states that ATF 4134 (MB-Approval 236.14) is compatible with the older 236.12 specification and is “specifically recommended for the 5-speed automatic transmission 722.6”, which means 236.10 / 236.12 / 236.14 can all be used in a 722.6.",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[1].trans": "722.9 (7G-TRONIC, early, before 2010-06)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[1].alternatives[0].brand": "Mercedes genuine",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[1].alternatives[0].product": "A0019896803 (genuine, 6803)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[1].note": "Important correction: not every 722.9 uses 236.15. The official PDF on bevo.mercedes-benz.com states that 236.14 applies to both the 722.6 and the 722.9, but not to the 7G-TRONIC PLUS. Genuine fluid is about 250 CNY/L at a 4S dealer and about 100 CNY/L on Taobao; Mobil ATF 134 works out at 418 CNY for an 18 L drum.",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[2].trans": "722.9 (7G-TRONIC PLUS, from 2010-06)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[2].note": "Fuchs's website notes that 7134 FE “may only be used for MB 236.15 and must not be mixed with other ATF specifications”; it is the NAG II+ factory fill.",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[3].trans": "725.0 (9G-TRONIC, 9-speed automatic)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[3].spec": "MB 236.17 (also usable in transmissions calling for 236.16)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[3].alternatives[0].product": "Shell Spirax D971 (same product as the factory fill, recommended for a drain and refill)",
  "CDATA.transmissionFluids[3].note": "A drain and refill without the torque converter takes about 6 L; including the converter it is about 9–10 L, and a 4S dealer will normally bill for 10 L. Owner measurement: a little over 5 L drained, 5 L added, then another 1 L after driving.",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[0].brand": "Bosch",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[0].note": "On JD, two 1 L bottles came to 61.51 CNY (about 30.8 CNY/L); equilibrium reflux boiling point ≥250 ℃, wet boiling point ≥160 ℃, interval 2 years or 40,000 km.",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[1].spec": "DOT4 Plus (Mercedes factory Blatt 331.0)",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[1].brand": "Mercedes genuine",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[1].note": "Genuine part numbers A0009890807 / A000989080711; the Russian sites quote no CNY price, hence the blank. A 4S change is about 400 CNY per time including labour, or about 100 CNY of labour at an independent if you supply the fluid.",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[2].spec": "DOT4 / DOT5.1 alternative",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[2].brand": "AISIN",
  "CDATA.brakeFluid[2].note": "An Autohome W205 owner supplied AISIN DOT5.1 and had it changed for 100 CNY of labour.",
